{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Good.</b> It is the word of the fool who says: enough for me is a handful of bread in tranquility, rather than two handfuls with toil and vexation of spirit — that a person should think about the future, what he will eat tomorrow, yet he does not know what a day will bring forth."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:28.984596072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}